id:                     E6400
trigger_tool:           SDL|Conan|shell|device-W3
phase:                  source-patch|consumer-test|target-validation
error_signature:        version-only consumer reported as native capability|callback buffer synthesized|dynamic core marker without guest execution|strtoull accepted signed or non-decimal backend hint

severity:               2
category:               testing, portability, runtime-capability, evidence
match_keywords:         SDL_VIDEODRIVER, nativewindow, OpenGLES2, SDL_RenderPresent, SDL_AUDIODRIVER, ohaudio, mixer output, callback observer, core=dynamic, guest sentinel, application-level probe, strtoull, positive decimal, lexical validation
title:                  Bind cross-platform capability probes to production backend boundaries

root_cause:             A version smoke test and provider-level header inspection can succeed while the packaged application never creates a native window, never delivers mixer PCM to a real audio callback, or falls back to the normal CPU core. Markers placed in a callback or emitted at process startup can also create false positives without proving the preceding production stages. Unsigned numeric conversion alone is also insufficient: strtoull accepts a leading minus sign and can turn it into an unsigned maximum, so backend identifiers and dimensions need an explicit decimal lexical guard.
affected_scope:         Cross-platform SDL or emulator packages whose adaptation claim includes native graphics, audio output, or architecture-specific execution and whose target provider is selected at runtime.
verification_cmd:       Build one installed application candidate; run separate video, audio, and dynamic-core invocations; require exact backend names, a marker after the production present/callback boundary, and a guest-produced sentinel; reject missing, dummy, offscreen, synthesized, static-only, signed, non-decimal, zero, and overflow tuple values.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           production-boundary-capability-probe
rec_description:        Gate probes with explicit test-only variables. Validate NativeWindow inputs before SDL initialization using a non-empty all-digits and positive-range parser, then emit a video marker only after SDL_RenderPresent or SDL_GL_SwapWindow. Inject a bounded signal at the application mixer output before final conversion and let the OHAudio callback read finite non-zero samples without writing. Select the dynamic core and require both its production entry marker and output from a guest command.
rec_command:            SDL_VIDEODRIVER=nativewindow SDL_RENDER_DRIVER=opengles2; SDL_AUDIODRIVER=ohaudio; core=dynamic with guest sentinel
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               production-source-and-consumer-harness

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      diagnostic-only-provider-probe
fallback_description:   Use a standalone SDL or provider fixture only to diagnose missing symbols or drivers. It cannot replace the application-level run and must not be counted as a capability pass.
fallback_command:       inspect frozen SDL_config.h and provider manifest; do not promote the result to application PASS
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          diagnostic-harness

forbid_1_pattern:       --version.*PASS.*video|SDL_GetCurrentVideoDriver.*startup.*PASS|strtoull.*no.*digit.*check
forbid_1_reason:        Version output or a driver-name read does not prove window, renderer, or frame presentation.
forbid_1_consequence:   A package can pass CI while NativeWindow/EGL initialization fails on the target compositor, or a malformed/negative tuple reaches the native backend.
forbid_2_pattern:       callback.*write.*silence|callback.*synthes|nonzero.*after.*fill
forbid_2_reason:        Writing the callback buffer manufactures PCM after the mixer boundary and hides a silent or bypassed application mixer.
forbid_2_consequence:   The test reports audio output even when OHAudio did not receive application-produced samples.
forbid_3_pattern:       dynrec.*marker.*without.*guest|static.*dynamic.*marker
forbid_3_reason:        A static log line or process startup does not prove dynamic translation or guest execution.
forbid_3_consequence:   An emulator that fell back to the normal core is misreported as architecture-specific support.

principles:             P005,P010,P013
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

